---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Terms of Use | Study Hub"
  description="Terms for accessing Study Hub learning resources, the document reader, AI study tools, and contribution features."
>
  <main class="legal-page">
    <header class="legal-page-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Using the learning library</p>
      <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
      <p>By using Study Hub, you agree to use the website and its learning materials responsibly and in accordance with these terms.</p>
      <p class="policy-updated">Last updated <time datetime="2026-10-10">October 10, 2026</time></p>
    </header>

    <article class="legal-copy">
      <section>
        <h2>1. About Study Hub</h2>
        <p>Study Hub provides educational subject pages, notes, past papers, document-reading tools, and related learning features. The site is intended to support independent study; it is not a school, examining body, or substitute for advice from a qualified teacher.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>2. Appropriate use</h2>
        <p>Use Study Hub lawfully and in a way that does not disrupt the service or other learners. Do not attempt unauthorized access, interfere with the site or its security controls, misuse forms, distribute malware, or use the site to violate another person’s rights.</p>
        <p>Do not copy, republish, sell, or distribute a resource unless you have permission or the law otherwise allows it. A file appearing in the library does not transfer ownership or grant a reuse licence.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>3. Learning resources and availability</h2>
        <p>Resources are provided for personal study and revision. Syllabuses, examination requirements, titles, and availability may change, and files or descriptions may contain errors. Check important academic requirements with your school and the relevant education authorities.</p>
        <p>Study Hub may update, move, restrict, or remove a page or resource to maintain the library, address a rights concern, or protect the service. We aim to keep the site useful but do not promise uninterrupted availability or that every resource will remain accessible.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>4. AI study companion</h2>
        <p>The AI study companion generates explanations from the PDF page and question you provide. AI output can be incomplete, incorrect, or unsuitable for a particular syllabus. Check answers independently and do not treat them as official examination guidance or professional advice.</p>
        <p>When you use the AI tool, the page image, question, and recent conversation context are processed by Study Hub’s AI service and an external AI provider. Do not submit confidential or personal information. See the <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '')}/privacy.html`}>Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>5. Suggestions and resource contributions</h2>
        <p>Submit only lawful content that you have the right to share. By offering a file, you confirm that you are permitted to provide it for review and possible inclusion in the library. A submission is not published automatically; Study Hub may review, decline, edit its catalogue description, or remove material.</p>
        <p>Do not submit private or sensitive information through suggestions or resource forms. See the <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '')}/copyright.html`}>Copyright Information</a> page for a way to raise a rights concern.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>6. External services and links</h2>
        <p>Study Hub may link to or embed material operated by other organisations. Those services have their own terms, privacy practices, and availability. A link or embed does not mean Study Hub controls or endorses the external service.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>7. Changes and contact</h2>
        <p>We may revise these terms as the site develops. The latest revision date appears above. Continued use after a revision means you accept the updated terms to the extent permitted by applicable law.</p>
        <p>For questions about these terms, email <a href="mailto:trusteth777@gmail.com">trusteth777@gmail.com</a>.</p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
